Yeah, I know, this *REALLY* annoyed me for a couple of games where I spent
hours attempting to climb back up. Eventually it works (you need a lot of
patience!). However I found a much easier method:


WARNING: Spoiler! (but you're going to read it anyway, aren't you?)




^L















Put on a ring of levitation when climbing back up through Gehennom. During my
last game, having a ring of levitation on caused me never to teleport to a
lower level when attempting to go back upstairs (wearing a ring of levitation
also gives you control of your motion while flying on the air elemental
level). The only problem is that sometimes, when you attempt to go upstairs,
you get teleported randomly elsewhere on the same level. Normally this is not
a problem, but if you're on one of the three levels with the Wizard's tower
and you get teleported inside it, you have to walk back down to the bottom
level, magic-portal out back to a deeper level, and try going back up again.
But it beats the hell out of going up one, down two, up one, down one, up
three, down two, etc...! Another warning: as some of your items get randomly
cursed because you're carrying the Amulet, your ring of levitation might
get cursed. It's a good idea to have holy water or remove curse scrolls handy
(otherwise you might end up starving for lack of being able to pick up a
corpse or food ration...).

Have fun climbing back up!

